---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import boardSignalSilence from "../assets/why-domain-expertise/board-signal-silence.jpg";
import signalIgnored from "../assets/why-domain-expertise/signal-ignored.png";
import { pageSeo } from "../seo/registry.mjs";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pageSeo["/why-domain-expertise-matters"]}>
	<main id="main" class="why-domain-page">
		<section class="opening section-rule">
			<div class="shell">
				<h1>Why domain expertise matters</h1>
				<p class="dek">People coaching teams should have expertise in the environment they are coaching. A credential from an outside body cannot confer that expertise. There is no substitute for developing expertise in the work.</p>
				<p class="display-line">In your business. Where ROI is measured in grip, not attendance.</p>
				<div class="problem">
					<p>Generic Agile supplied vocabulary. It did not teach <span class="heat">this backlog</span>, <span class="heat">this intake</span>, <span class="heat">this decision</span>, or <span class="heat">this quality bar</span>. It was not in your domain. It was <span class="strike">decoration</span>. Your domain is not decoration. Your business matters. The credential did not transfer to the context in which you operate. That is the whole problem.</p>
					<p>People without domain expertise still get put next to teams. They arrive with a credential from outside. They cannot see the work. They still talk. They still schedule. They still rearrange the ritual. The team has to translate the business for them. Then the credential is treated as if it outranks the work. That is backwards. It does not help the team. That is harmful.</p>
					<p>They also bring framework load. Generic vocabulary, ceremonies, roles, and rules begin competing with the work for the team's attention. A framework should help people see the work and make better decisions. It should not become another system the team has to perform for. When too much attention goes into maintaining the framework, less attention remains for the demand, the quality, the decisions, and the work itself. That is another way teams lose grip.</p>
					<p class="framework-emphasis">Use only enough framework to help the work move.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section section-rule" aria-labelledby="get-in-title">
			<div class="shell split-section">
				<h2 id="get-in-title">Get in the work or get out</h2>
				<div class="section-body">
					<p>Companies rent coaches who are not in the work, not in the tools, and not in the business. Those people stay involved. They comment. They schedule. They do not get the work done. When they leave, the organization discovers the skill did not leave with them. It was never there. What looked like capability was coverage.</p>
					<p>There is no useful middle state called involved. A person is committed to getting the work done, or they are not. If they cannot open the board, read the ticket, sit in the refinement, and help the team move, they are not a coach here.</p>
					<div class="posters">
						<p class="poster"><span class="poster-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span><span class="poster-label">Get in the work.</span></p>
						<p class="poster"><span class="poster-num" aria-hidden="true">02</span><span class="poster-label">Or get out.</span></p>
					</div>
					<p class="section-verdict">Commentary is not a role. Wall decoration is not a role.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section section-rule" aria-labelledby="board-title">
			<div class="shell split-section">
				<h2 id="board-title">The board tells the truth. Or it performs.</h2>
				<div class="section-body">
					<p>The board can tell you what is happening. Or it can perform control for an audience. Domain expertise is what lets someone tell the difference. You need people who can read the board and say what is actually happening in the work. Not people who tidy it until the evidence goes quiet.</p>
					<p>We have watched teams sterilize the signal. Clean tickets. Pretty columns. No fight in the data. The work is slipping, and the board has been made presentable enough that nobody has to hear it. That is not grip. That is the sound of silence.</p>
					<p>Someone with true domain expertise does the opposite. They keep the signal loud enough to act on. They bring the team and the work into focus because they understand the domain, the constraints, and what good looks like.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<figure class="shell editorial-figure board-figure">
				<Image
					src={boardSignalSilence}
					alt="A wall crowded with work notes beside a wall where the same information has been arranged into a clean grid."
					widths={[720, 960, 1280, 1600]}
					sizes="(max-width: 720px) calc(100vw - 32px), min(1180px, calc(100vw - 48px))"
					layout="constrained"
				/>
				<figcaption class="caption-pair">
					<span><strong class="caption-lead">Signal.</strong> The constraint is still visible.</span>
					<span><strong class="caption-lead">Silence.</strong> Made presentable.</span>
				</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</section>

		<section class="section section-rule" aria-labelledby="team-boundary-title">
			<div class="shell split-section">
				<h2 id="team-boundary-title">The first boundary that matters is the team</h2>
				<div class="section-body">
					<p>Domain expertise matters here because this is where the work is real. A credential does not show up in a team. Grip does.</p>
					<p>A team with the expertise in the room can take on difficult work, surface problems early, make more decisions where the work happens, and keep moving without an outsider translating the business for them. That is the first place you can tell whether the claim is true.</p>
					<p>If the team still has to explain the work to the person standing next to it, the expertise is not in the domain. It is coverage.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section section-rule" aria-labelledby="hands-judgment-title">
			<div class="shell split-section">
				<h2 id="hands-judgment-title">Hands in the work, and the judgment to develop others</h2>
				<div class="section-body">
					<p>Domain expertise matters because the work requires both. Sometimes someone has to question, mentor, and help another person reason through a hard problem. Sometimes someone has to put their hands in the work and help do it.</p>
					<p>A person who only comments cannot do that. A person who only takes over cannot do that either. Both moves require knowing the domain well enough to judge which one the situation needs, and then develop the next person already in the work.</p>
					<p>That is the capability that has to stay inside the company.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section" aria-labelledby="working-title">
			<div class="shell split-section">
				<h2 id="working-title">How you would know it is working</h2>
				<div class="section-body">
					<p>Attendance is not evidence. Grip is evidence.</p>
					<p>The team is the first useful boundary. Ready work before planning. Fewer interruptions. Ownership that does not bounce. Hidden work visible early. Quality that does not arrive as a late surprise. People who can run planning or refinement without an outsider in the room.</p>
					<p>Those signs mean execution is changing. They are not the finish line. The work still has to survive the marketplace.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<figure class="shell editorial-figure beacon-figure">
				<Image
					src={signalIgnored}
					alt="Two warning beacons, one lit amber and one covered with black tape."
					widths={[720, 960, 1280, 1600]}
					sizes="(max-width: 720px) calc(100vw - 32px), min(1180px, calc(100vw - 48px))"
					layout="constrained"
				/>
				<figcaption>The signal being ignored.</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</section>

		<section class="close-band">
			<div class="shell close-inner">
				<p class="close-lead">Start a conversation about your domain and who is actually in the work.</p>
				<p class="close-bound">No transformation pitch. No universal answer. Your backlog. Your intake. Your quality bar.</p>
				<p class="close-action"><a class="button" href="/contact/">Start a conversation</a></p>
				<p class="close-links">
					<a class="text-link" href="/grip-check/">Check Your Grip</a>
					<a class="quiet-link" href="/domain-guides/">Domain Guides</a>
				</p>
				<p class="close-final">If the skill has to live in the team and be renewed from within, that is Domain Guides.</p>
				<p class="close-final">The skill stays where it belongs. In your business.</p>
				<p class="close-final">ROI is measured in grip, not attendance.</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
	.why-domain-page {
		overflow: clip;
		background: var(--paper);
	}

	.opening { padding: 108px 0 92px; }
	.opening h1 {
		max-width: none;
		margin-bottom: 28px;
		font-size: clamp(3.7rem, 8.4vw, 5.7rem);
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-heavy);
		line-height: 1.04;
		letter-spacing: -0.028em;
	}
	.dek {
		max-width: 42rem;
		margin-bottom: 42px;
		color: var(--charcoal);
		font-size: clamp(1.28rem, 2.1vw, 1.55rem);
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
		line-height: 1.38;
	}
	.display-line {
		max-width: none;
		margin: 0 0 56px;
		padding-top: 18px;
		border-top: 4px solid var(--amber);
		color: var(--amber-text);
		font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 3.2vw, 2.35rem);
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-heavy);
		line-height: 1.15;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}
	.problem {
		max-width: 46rem;
		padding: 6px 0 6px 22px;
		border-left: 6px solid var(--amber);
	}
	.problem p {
		margin-bottom: 1.1em;
		color: var(--charcoal);
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
	}
	.problem p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

	.heat, .strike {
		padding: 0 0.06em;
		outline: none;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}
	.heat {
		box-decoration-break: clone;
		-webkit-box-decoration-break: clone;
		background: transparent;
		box-shadow: inset 0 -0.38em 0 var(--amber);
	}
	.strike {
		text-decoration: line-through;
		text-decoration-color: var(--amber);
		text-decoration-thickness: 3px;
		text-underline-offset: 0;
	}

	.split-section {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
		gap: clamp(42px, 8vw, 128px);
		align-items: start;
		margin-bottom: 48px;
	}
	.split-section h2 {
		margin-bottom: 0;
		padding-bottom: 18px;
		border-bottom: 2px solid var(--charcoal);
	}
	.section-body p {
		max-width: 38rem;
		margin-bottom: 1.1em;
		color: var(--charcoal);
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
	}
	.section-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
	.framework-emphasis, .section-body .section-verdict { font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); }
	.evidence-list {
		max-width: 38rem;
		margin: 0 0 1.1em;
		padding-left: 1.2em;
		color: var(--charcoal);
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
	}
	.evidence-list li { margin-bottom: 0.2em; }

	.posters {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		grid-auto-rows: 1fr;
		gap: 18px;
		align-items: stretch;
		margin: 36px 0 28px;
	}
	.poster {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-rows: auto 1fr;
		height: 100%;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 28px 24px 24px;
		border: 3px solid var(--amber);
		background: var(--reading);
		transition: transform 160ms ease-out, background-color 160ms ease-out, box-shadow 160ms ease-out;
	}
	@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
		.poster:hover {
		background: var(--amber-wash);
		box-shadow: inset 0 3px 0 var(--amber);
		transform: translateY(-2px);
		}
	}
	.poster-num {
		display: block;
		margin-bottom: 18px;
		color: var(--amber-text);
		font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.6rem);
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-heavy);
		line-height: 0.9;
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
	}
	.poster-label {
		display: block;
		color: var(--charcoal);
		font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.4vw, 1.75rem);
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-heavy);
		line-height: 1.15;
	}

	.editorial-figure {
		margin: 0 auto;
	}
	.editorial-figure :global(img) {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
	}
	.editorial-figure figcaption {
		margin-top: 8px;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		font-size: 1rem;
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
		line-height: 1.4;
	}
	.caption-pair {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 18px;
	}
	.caption-lead { font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); }

	.close-band {
		padding: 118px 0;
		background: var(--charcoal);
		color: var(--paper);
		border-top: 4px solid var(--amber);
		border-bottom: 5px solid var(--amber);
	}
	.close-inner {
		max-width: 790px;
		padding-left: clamp(22px, 4vw, 48px);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--amber);
	}
	.close-lead {
		margin-bottom: 22px;
		color: var(--paper);
		font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.2vw, 2.4rem);
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-heavy);
		line-height: 1.18;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}
	.close-bound {
		max-width: 38rem;
		margin-bottom: 32px;
		color: var(--paper);
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
	}
	.close-action { margin-bottom: 28px; }
	.close-links {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 22px 36px;
		align-items: center;
		margin-bottom: 36px;
	}
	.text-link, .quiet-link {
		position: relative;
		color: var(--paper);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.text-link::after, .quiet-link::after {
		position: absolute;
		right: 0;
		bottom: -5px;
		left: 0;
		height: 2px;
		background: var(--amber);
		content: "";
		transform: scaleX(0);
		transform-origin: left;
		transition: transform 160ms ease-out;
	}
	.text-link {
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
	}
	.quiet-link {
		color: var(--paper);
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
	}
	.text-link:hover, .quiet-link:hover {
		color: var(--paper);
	}
	.text-link:hover::after, .quiet-link:hover::after {
		transform: scaleX(1);
	}
	.close-final {
		max-width: 38rem;
		margin-bottom: 0;
		color: var(--paper);
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
		line-height: 1.5;
	}
	.close-final + .close-final { margin-top: 8px; }

	@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
		.heat {
			background: transparent;
			box-shadow: inset 0 -0.38em 0 transparent;
			transition: background-color 160ms ease-out, box-shadow 160ms ease-out;
		}
		.heat:hover {
			background: var(--amber-wash);
			box-shadow: inset 0 -0.38em 0 var(--amber);
		}
		.strike {
			text-decoration-color: transparent;
			transition: text-decoration-color 160ms ease-out;
		}
		.strike:hover {
			text-decoration-color: var(--amber);
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.opening { padding: 84px 0 64px; }
		.opening h1 { letter-spacing: -0.022em; }
		.display-line { margin-bottom: 40px; }
		.split-section {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 18px;
			margin-bottom: 32px;
		}
		.posters { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
		.caption-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; }
		.close-band { padding: 82px 0; }
	}

	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
		.poster, .heat, .strike, .text-link::after, .quiet-link::after { transition: none; }
		.poster:hover { transform: none; }
	}
</style>
